  "lyrics": [
    {
      "start": 0.05,
      "end": 3.458,
      "text": "A foreign key does not only check new child rows.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 3.458,
      "end": 7.43,
      "text": "It also decides what happens when the parent moves or leaves.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 7.43,
      "end": 13.611,
      "text": "ON DELETE RESTRICT or NO ACTION refuses to delete a parent that still has children.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 13.611,
      "end": 18.638,
      "text": "That is the safe default in spirit, even when the dialect wording differs.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 18.638,
      "end": 21.513,
      "text": "Maya still has orders, so Maya stays.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 21.513,
      "end": 24.597,
      "text": "ON DELETE CASCADE deletes the children too.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 24.597,
      "end": 27.819,
      "text": "Delete the order, and the order lines go with it.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 27.819,
      "end": 29.68,
      "text": "That matches a weak entity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 29.68,
      "end": 31.472,
      "text": "It is violent on a customer.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 31.472,
      "end": 36.402,
      "text": "Do not cascade a customer delete unless you truly mean to erase history.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 36.402,
      "end": 40.388,
      "text": "ON DELETE SET NULL clears the pointer and keeps the child.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 40.388,
      "end": 43.069,
      "text": "The order remains, with no customer.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 43.069,
      "end": 44.944,
      "text": "The column must allow NULL.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 44.944,
      "end": 48.916,
      "text": "ON DELETE SET DEFAULT writes the default value instead.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 48.916,
      "end": 53.013,
      "text": "Useful when a placeholder parent exists, rare otherwise.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 53.013,
      "end": 57.666,
      "text": "ON UPDATE CASCADE copies a changed parent key into the children.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 57.666,
      "end": 61.166,
      "text": "If you never change primary keys, you barely need it.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 61.166,
      "end": 64.583,
      "text": "That is one more reason to prefer dull surrogates.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 64.583,
      "end": 68.319,
      "text": "Write the action next to the foreign key, not in a wiki.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 68.319,
      "end": 70.527,
      "text": "The engine will not read the wiki.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 70.527,
      "end": 73.791,
      "text": "Different relationships deserve different actions.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 73.791,
      "end": 76.777,
      "text": "order_lines cascade from orders.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 76.777,
      "end": 79.041,
      "text": "orders restrict from customers.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 79.041,
      "end": 83.305,
      "text": "credentials cascade from customers if you treat them as a part.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 83.305,
      "end": 84.833,
      "text": "Think in sentences.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 84.833,
      "end": 89.0,
      "text": "When an order disappears, its lines were never independent.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 89.0,
      "end": 96.569,
      "text": "When a customer disappears, the orders are history, so refuse, or archive, or soft-delete instead.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 96.569,
      "end": 101.222,
      "text": "Soft-delete is an application pattern: a deleted_at column.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 101.222,
      "end": 103.208,
      "text": "It is not an ON DELETE action.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 103.208,
      "end": 105.236,
      "text": "Do not mix them without a plan.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 105.236,
      "end": 107.486,
      "text": "Test the action with two rows.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 107.486,
      "end": 108.819,
      "text": "Delete the parent.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 108.819,
      "end": 112.555,
      "text": "See whether the child vanished, blocked, or went null.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 112.555,
      "end": 114.236,
      "text": "Then keep that behavior.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 114.236,
      "end": 118.666,
      "text": "ON DELETE CASCADE on a tall tree can remove more than you see.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 118.666,
      "end": 125.416,
      "text": "A customer cascade that also cascades orders that cascade lines that cascade shipments is a cliff.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 125.416,
      "end": 127.75,
      "text": "Draw the cliff before you enable it.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 127.75,
      "end": 131.569,
      "text": "RESTRICT two levels up even if the bottom cascades.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 131.569,
      "end": 134.444,
      "text": "NO ACTION and RESTRICT are close.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 134.444,
      "end": 139.305,
      "text": "The difference is when the check runs, especially with deferred constraints.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 139.305,
      "end": 141.833,
      "text": "In classroom SQL they feel the same.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 141.833,
      "end": 144.347,
      "text": "In a long transaction they might not.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 144.347,
      "end": 147.375,
      "text": "SET NULL can surprise a NOT NULL you forgot.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 147.375,
      "end": 151.013,
      "text": "The ALTER will fail, or the delete will fail later.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 151.013,
      "end": 152.444,
      "text": "Pair them on purpose.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 152.444,
      "end": 156.055,
      "text": "Some teams never cascade from an application user.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 156.055,
      "end": 162.222,
      "text": "They delete children in a script, then delete the parent, all inside one transaction.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 162.222,
      "end": 166.68,
      "text": "The foreign key still RESTRICT, which catches a missed child table.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 166.68,
      "end": 168.388,
      "text": "That is a valid policy.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 168.388,
      "end": 170.638,
      "text": "The engine is the last reviewer.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 170.638,
      "end": 174.347,
      "text": "Triggers that delete children are a homemade cascade.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 174.347,
      "end": 178.111,
      "text": "Prefer the declared action unless you need extra logging.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 178.111,
      "end": 181.763,
      "text": "Logging can live in a trigger that does not replace the action.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 181.763,
      "end": 183.263,
      "text": "Document the cliff.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 183.263,
      "end": 184.666,
      "text": "Test it on a copy.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 184.666,
      "end": 187.097,
      "text": "Then the production delete is boring.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 187.097,
      "end": 188.847,
      "text": "Boring deletes are the goal.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 188.847,
      "end": 194.958,
      "text": "Actions are how you choose the boredom: refuse, take the children, or drop the pointer.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 194.958,
      "end": 196.138,
      "text": "Pick per arrow.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 196.138,
      "end": 197.805,
      "text": "Write it in the constraint.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 197.805,
      "end": 198.625,
      "text": "Sleep.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 198.625,
      "end": 201.263,
      "text": "An action is a story about grief.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 201.263,
      "end": 202.638,
      "text": "The parent is gone.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 202.638,
      "end": 206.875,
      "text": "Do the children vanish, stay unnamed, or block the funeral?",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 206.875,
      "end": 208.638,
      "text": "Pick the story per arrow.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 208.638,
      "end": 211.25,
      "text": "Do not inherit CASCADE from a snippet.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 211.25,
      "end": 214.097,
      "text": "Snippets do not know your history table.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 214.097,
      "end": 215.555,
      "text": "Restrict history.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 215.555,
      "end": 216.93,
      "text": "Cascade parts.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 216.93,
      "end": 220.027,
      "text": "Null only when unnamed is a real state.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 220.027,
      "end": 223.041,
      "text": "Test with two rows, not with production.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 223.041,
      "end": 225.597,
      "text": "Read the row counts after the delete.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 225.597,
      "end": 228.416,
      "text": "Keep the story that matches those counts.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 228.416,
      "end": 230.708,
      "text": "Write the story in the constraint.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 230.708,
      "end": 233.027,
      "text": "Then a new engineer will not guess.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 233.027,
      "end": 235.361,
      "text": "Guessing is how cliffs get steeper.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 235.361,
      "end": 237.708,
      "text": "Declared actions are the railing.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 237.708,
      "end": 243.694,
      "text": "A foreign key is a link: one or more columns in a child that reference a parent's key.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 243.694,
      "end": 247.486,
      "text": "A review points at a product and may also point at a user.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 247.486,
      "end": 250.472,
      "text": "Two foreign keys on one child is normal.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 250.472,
      "end": 252.18,
      "text": "Name each constraint.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 252.18,
      "end": 263.722,
      "text": "CONSTRAINT reviews_product_fk FOREIGN KEY (product_id) REFERENCES products (product_id) is a sentence the engine can run.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 263.722,
      "end": 272.777,
      "text": "The default referential action is NO ACTION or RESTRICT, depending on dialect: refuse the parent change if children exist.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 272.777,
      "end": 278.263,
      "text": "That default is how you do not evaporate history by deleting a product someone reviewed.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 278.378,
      "end": 282.855,
      "text": "ON DELETE CASCADE deletes matching children when the parent goes.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 282.855,
      "end": 292.411,
      "text": "Use it when the child cannot exist without the parent and you mean to destroy the whole bundle: order lines when an unfinished order is discarded.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 292.411,
      "end": 295.994,
      "text": "Do not cascade a product into a year of invoices.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 295.994,
      "end": 300.703,
      "text": "ON DELETE SET NULL clears the child's pointer and keeps the child row.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 300.703,
      "end": 306.716,
      "text": "Reviews might remain as anonymous text if a user is removed and the business allows it.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 306.716,
      "end": 308.591,
      "text": "The column must allow NULL.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 308.591,
      "end": 315.064,
      "text": "ON DELETE SET DEFAULT points the child at a declared default parent, such as a placeholder user.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 315.064,
      "end": 320.203,
      "text": "ON UPDATE CASCADE rewrites the copied key if the parent's key changes.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 320.203,
      "end": 325.508,
      "text": "If your primary keys are dull and never edited, you will barely need ON UPDATE.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 325.508,
      "end": 327.966,
      "text": "That is a reason dull keys are kind.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 327.966,
      "end": 334.466,
      "text": "If you used a natural key people edit, ON UPDATE CASCADE is a moving truck for every child.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 334.466,
      "end": 336.828,
      "text": "Prefer not to move the house numbers.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 336.828,
      "end": 339.591,
      "text": "Prefer a surrogate that never changes.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 339.591,
      "end": 350.064,
      "text": "Match the action to the sentence in requirements: when a parent leaves, children vanish, children stay with a hole, or the parent is not allowed to leave.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 350.064,
      "end": 352.369,
      "text": "Write that sentence in the constraint.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 352.369,
      "end": 358.341,
      "text": "Test it: insert parent, insert child, delete parent, SELECT the child.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 358.341,
      "end": 363.244,
      "text": "If the child is gone and you wanted a hole, you cascaded by mistake.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 363.244,
      "end": 368.341,
      "text": "If the delete errors and you wanted a bundle gone, you restricted by mistake.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 368.341,
      "end": 371.411,
      "text": "Multiple children mean multiple policies.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 371.411,
      "end": 373.064,
      "text": "Payments might restrict.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 373.064,
      "end": 374.966,
      "text": "Draft lines might cascade.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 374.966,
      "end": 378.758,
      "text": "Do not pick one action for the whole database out of fashion.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 378.758,
      "end": 380.328,
      "text": "Pick per relationship.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 380.328,
      "end": 385.286,
      "text": "SQLite still needs foreign keys enabled or none of the actions run.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 385.286,
      "end": 389.564,
      "text": "Turn them on in every connection that should obey the design.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 389.564,
      "end": 395.494,
      "text": "Then delete and update are part of the schema, not a scavenger hunt in application code.",
      "slide": ""
    }
  ]
}
